{
  "_what": "What scripts/deploy.sh (node-config 0d45b51) DECIDES, produced by EXECUTING its own grep/sed/python pipelines verbatim against testdata/node_state.json. Not written by hand and not read off the source.",
  "_env": "Produced under env -i with no LANG, which is what host/deploy-watch/node.deploywatch.plist gives the real deploy: that plist sets PATH and nothing else, and launchctl getenv LANG is empty. It matters. sort(1) collates by locale, so an interactive en_US.UTF-8 shell orders redash_db BEFORE redash-db while the C locale launchd provides orders it after. The bash deploy therefore never had one stable order; the Python is byte-ordered, which is the launchd one, which is the one production has always run.",
  "_why": "This port claims behavioral equivalence. A live A/B is not available - running the real deploy twice against production is exactly the thing that must not happen - so the decisions are extracted, pinned here, and asserted against the Python in test_equivalence.py.",
